TASK 7 – Override and Specialise Behaviour (4 Marks)
1. Method Overriding
Method overriding allows a subclass to provide its own implementation of a method inherited from the parent class.
In the Parking Management System, different vehicles may have different parking fees. Therefore, calculateFee() is overridden in Car, Bike and Bus classes.
2. Java Program Using @Override
class Vehicle {
    String vehicleNo;
    Vehicle(String vehicleNo) {
        this.vehicleNo = vehicleNo;
    }
    double calculateFee() {
        return 50;
    }
    @Override
    public String toString() {
        return "Vehicle Number: " + vehicleNo;
    }
    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object obj) {
        if (this == obj)
            return true;
        if (!(obj instanceof Vehicle))
            return false;
        Vehicle v = (Vehicle) obj;
        return vehicleNo.equals(v.vehicleNo);
    }
    @Override
    public int hashCode() {
        return vehicleNo.hashCode();
    }
}
class Car extends Vehicle {
    Car(String vehicleNo) {
        super(vehicleNo);
    }
    @Override
    double calculateFee() {
        return 100;
    }
}
class Bike extends Vehicle {
    Bike(String vehicleNo) {
        super(vehicleNo);
    }
    @Override
    double calculateFee() {
        return 30;
    }
}
class Bus extends Vehicle {
    Bus(String vehicleNo) {
        super(vehicleNo);
    }
    @Override
    double calculateFee() {
        return 150;
    }
}
class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Vehicle v1 = new Car("TN01AB1234");
        Vehicle v2 = new Bike("TN02CD5678");

        System.out.println(v1.calculateFee());
        System.out.println(v2.calculateFee());
        System.out.println(v1);
    }
}
3. Rules of Method Overriding
1.	The method name and parameter list must be the same.
2.	The return type must be the same or compatible (covariant).
3.	The subclass cannot reduce the access level of the overridden method.
4.	@Override annotation identifies overridden methods and helps detect mistakes.
4. Use of final Keyword
Usage	Purpose
final variable	Prevents changing the assigned value.
final method	Prevents subclasses from overriding the method.
final class	Prevents inheritance.
Example:
final int MAX_SLOTS = 100;
This ensures that the maximum slot limit cannot be reassigned.
5. Object Class Methods
•	toString(): Returns vehicle details as a String.
•	equals(): Compares two vehicles using registration numbers.
•	hashCode(): Generates the same hash code for vehicles with equal registration numbers.
Therefore, two Vehicle objects with the same registration number are treated as equal.
6. Alternative Concept – Switch vs Method Overriding
Comparison	Method Overriding	Switch Statement
Fee calculation	Each subclass calculates its fee.	One method checks vehicle type.
Adding new vehicle type	Create a new subclass.	Add a new case.
Time complexity	O(1)	O(1)
Code maintenance	Easier to extend.	Requires modifying switch logic.
Classes changed	Usually only the new subclass.	Vehicle fee calculation class must change.

